  "full_text": "So someone had a shirt that said, ducks will do it with anybody, or no, ducks just do it. You know, maybe the issue is, you know, I don't know about reincarnation, but like, the idea of do it like acting like yourself. How about that? Because like, if you're acting like somebody who you're not, then maybe it's going to lose your soul. But if you're acting like who you are, you know, like, I don't know. Like, some people are mean or something, or paranoid or something. Some people are very open, like friend or enemy, you know, whatever. Like, I don't know. Some people are very selective, picky. Some people are not very picky. And maybe you'll be judged on if you are yourself or you're somebody else. You know what I mean? If you're not yourself, the safest thing is to be yourself. How about that? Maybe not. I just got unfriendly. Safest thing is to do it the Roman Catholic way. Anyway, what?",
